1
00:00:01,106 --> 00:00:04,026
[microphone feedback]

2
00:00:04,109 --> 00:00:06,111
[♪ opening theme music playing]

3
00:00:40,646 --> 00:00:44,066
FLEX X COP 2

4
00:00:44,149 --> 00:00:46,902
CHARACTERS, PLACES, ORGANIZATIONS,
AND EVENTS IN THIS DRAMA ARE FICTITIOUS

5
00:00:46,985 --> 00:00:49,071
ALL CHILD ACTORS AND ANIMALS
FILMED IN A SAFE ENVIRONMENT

6
00:00:52,157 --> 00:00:53,658
[mouse clicking]

7
00:00:57,204 --> 00:00:59,456
Jin Isoo is late today.
We had a drink yesterday.

8
00:00:59,539 --> 00:01:00,624
Did you?

9
00:01:01,041 --> 00:01:02,709
[exhales] He must've lost again.

10
00:01:02,959 --> 00:01:04,336
EPISODE 11

11
00:01:07,631 --> 00:01:08,924
-Oh.
-[Changun] Uh...

12
00:01:09,675 --> 00:01:10,676
Detective Joo.

13
00:01:11,843 --> 00:01:13,887
We got a report from Jin Isoo's house.

14
00:01:13,970 --> 00:01:15,013
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

15
00:01:15,097 --> 00:01:16,473
You should go check it out.

16
00:01:21,228 --> 00:01:22,813
[tires screeching]

17
00:01:31,738 --> 00:01:32,906
This way, please.

18
00:01:34,866 --> 00:01:37,035
[♪ suspenseful, foreboding music playing]

19
00:02:02,686 --> 00:02:04,062
[Younghwan laughing] <i>Huh?</i>

20
00:02:04,146 --> 00:02:06,440
<i>My friend, Jin Isoo. </i>[laughs]

21
00:02:07,732 --> 00:02:08,900
[Isoo] <i>Younghwan, you, again!</i>

22
00:02:09,609 --> 00:02:10,610
You want to try, too?

23
00:02:10,694 --> 00:02:12,612
No! Please... Don't!

24
00:02:12,696 --> 00:02:15,657
I told you I'd never see you
if you did it again.

25
00:02:21,997 --> 00:02:24,374
<i>You should undergo</i>
<i>a proper investigation and quit drugs.</i>

26
00:02:24,458 --> 00:02:27,878
All my life,
I've never thought of you as a friend.

27
00:02:28,920 --> 00:02:30,756
[♪ tense, pulsating music playing]

28
00:02:43,351 --> 00:02:44,352
Jin Isoo.

29
00:02:49,566 --> 00:02:50,984
[♪ music swells]

30
00:03:02,496 --> 00:03:03,789
[♪ music resumes tempo]

31
00:03:12,881 --> 00:03:14,424
That's Kim Younghwan.

32
00:03:14,508 --> 00:03:16,134
[♪ music increases in tempo]

33
00:03:18,303 --> 00:03:19,429
What happened?

34
00:03:35,153 --> 00:03:36,446
[♪ music swells]

35
00:03:40,659 --> 00:03:41,868
[♪ music fades]

36
00:03:41,952 --> 00:03:43,328
[♪ ominous music playing]

37
00:03:44,538 --> 00:03:45,872
[camera shutter clicking]

38
00:03:55,048 --> 00:03:56,299
[♪ music fades]

39
00:03:58,426 --> 00:04:00,720
Do you two know who the victim is?

40
00:04:01,471 --> 00:04:03,265
He's Isoo's friend from middle school.

41
00:04:03,974 --> 00:04:06,351
He was the CEO
of the production company Isoo owns.

42
00:04:06,434 --> 00:04:08,270
Isoo personally arrested him for drugs.

43
00:04:08,353 --> 00:04:11,064
I looked into it,
and he was released two months ago.

44
00:04:17,153 --> 00:04:18,321
What happened?

45
00:04:19,030 --> 00:04:21,366
What time did you get home
after we split up?

46
00:04:25,495 --> 00:04:27,873
I think it was after 10:00 p.m.

47
00:04:27,956 --> 00:04:29,291
And then?

48
00:04:30,208 --> 00:04:31,710
[♪ gripping, suspenseful music playing]

49
00:04:31,793 --> 00:04:33,086
[sighs softly]

50
00:04:46,057 --> 00:04:47,225
[digital lock beeps]

51
00:04:48,852 --> 00:04:50,103
[Younghwan laughing]

52
00:04:50,186 --> 00:04:52,564
Look who's here!

53
00:04:52,647 --> 00:04:54,316
My friend, Jin Isoo!

54
00:04:57,193 --> 00:04:58,987
I've been waiting for you.

55
00:04:59,070 --> 00:05:01,031
What took you so long?

56
00:05:01,114 --> 00:05:02,282
How did you...

57
00:05:04,492 --> 00:05:06,119
[chuckles softly]

58
00:05:06,202 --> 00:05:07,495
I gave you a key before.

59
00:05:07,579 --> 00:05:09,539
[chuckles] Exactly.

60
00:05:10,498 --> 00:05:13,084
To your best friend. Did you forget?

61
00:05:14,920 --> 00:05:16,838
Wait a minute, you bastard.

62
00:05:17,714 --> 00:05:21,509
Did you erase
my very existence from your memory?

63
00:05:21,593 --> 00:05:23,929
Yes, I did.

64
00:05:24,012 --> 00:05:25,263
So just leave.

65
00:05:27,015 --> 00:05:29,225
Come on, don't be like that. It hurts.

66
00:05:30,018 --> 00:05:32,145
Just come sit down.

67
00:05:32,771 --> 00:05:33,772
Uh...

68
00:05:36,858 --> 00:05:39,945
[sighs] You did a fine job making this.

69
00:05:40,028 --> 00:05:41,821
It's classy.

70
00:05:41,905 --> 00:05:43,615
Tasty, too. [chuckles]

71
00:05:47,327 --> 00:05:48,745
What are you playing at?

72
00:05:48,828 --> 00:05:51,247
Your friend came to visit, you asshole.

73
00:05:51,331 --> 00:05:53,083
Let's have a drink like old times.

74
00:05:55,710 --> 00:05:57,212
Drink up.

75
00:05:58,797 --> 00:05:59,965
[sighs softly]

76
00:06:02,384 --> 00:06:03,468
[exhales sharply]

77
00:06:04,552 --> 00:06:05,845
Didn't you miss me?

78
00:06:08,139 --> 00:06:09,349
Finish your drink and go.

79
00:06:10,100 --> 00:06:11,267
As for me,

80
00:06:13,144 --> 00:06:15,480
I thought about you a lot.

81
00:06:17,899 --> 00:06:20,694
ONE WEEK EARLIER

82
00:06:20,777 --> 00:06:21,987
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

83
00:06:28,743 --> 00:06:29,786
Hey.

84
00:06:32,706 --> 00:06:34,833
Were you the one
who came in here last week?

85
00:06:34,916 --> 00:06:36,459
[chuckling]

86
00:06:36,543 --> 00:06:38,211
Bingo!

87
00:06:38,294 --> 00:06:39,629
[laughs smugly]

88
00:06:41,381 --> 00:06:44,092
I came because I missed you so much.

89
00:06:46,553 --> 00:06:51,766
You didn't even visit me in prison,
or bother to come the day I got out.

90
00:06:55,019 --> 00:06:57,439
If you were the one to put me away,

91
00:06:57,522 --> 00:06:59,941
the least you could've done
was check in on me.

92
00:07:00,817 --> 00:07:03,778
After all those years I spent
as your damn sidekick.

93
00:07:05,697 --> 00:07:08,616
No matter how hard I try,
I can't get over it.

94
00:07:09,284 --> 00:07:10,535
But what do you know?

95
00:07:12,287 --> 00:07:13,997
[vocalizing victory fanfare]

96
00:07:15,749 --> 00:07:17,208
[laughs smugly]

97
00:07:17,292 --> 00:07:19,586
I have a key to your house.

98
00:07:21,296 --> 00:07:23,256
[breathes deeply]

99
00:07:24,132 --> 00:07:26,342
You knocked yourself out
with sleeping pills

100
00:07:26,426 --> 00:07:28,386
and couldn't remember a damn thing.

101
00:07:28,470 --> 00:07:29,554
[♪ music swells]

102
00:07:30,764 --> 00:07:32,056
[♪ ominous music playing]

103
00:07:39,022 --> 00:07:40,440
MR. JIN ISOO

104
00:07:55,330 --> 00:07:57,665
You're nothing, you piece of shit.

105
00:07:59,667 --> 00:08:01,461
[♪ tense, ominous music playing]

106
00:08:18,978 --> 00:08:20,021
[blunt thud]

107
00:08:22,065 --> 00:08:23,399
[clattering]

108
00:08:23,483 --> 00:08:25,193
-[exclaims]
-[glass shattering]

109
00:08:25,276 --> 00:08:26,444
[exclaims]

110
00:08:26,945 --> 00:08:28,321
[breathing heavily]

111
00:08:33,117 --> 00:08:34,244
[shatters]

112
00:08:34,577 --> 00:08:36,788
[laughing maniacally]

113
00:08:36,871 --> 00:08:38,039
[♪ music swells]

114
00:08:38,122 --> 00:08:40,166
[exclaims, continues laughing]

115
00:08:41,042 --> 00:08:43,378
I could have killed you.

116
00:08:43,461 --> 00:08:45,713
[♪ suspenseful, foreboding music playing]

117
00:08:49,092 --> 00:08:51,511
I sent you to prison
to straighten you out,

118
00:08:51,594 --> 00:08:52,720
but you came back worse.

119
00:08:54,556 --> 00:08:55,557
Hey,

120
00:08:55,640 --> 00:08:57,767
get up and leave while I'm being nice.

121
00:08:58,935 --> 00:08:59,936
What about you?

122
00:09:03,940 --> 00:09:06,359
What would happen

123
00:09:06,442 --> 00:09:09,445
if the great Jin Isoo ended up in prison?

124
00:09:10,321 --> 00:09:13,283
[scoffs] Now that would be
quite a sight, right?

125
00:09:13,366 --> 00:09:15,827
Cut the crap and get up.

126
00:09:18,913 --> 00:09:20,123
Do I have to drag you out?

127
00:09:20,206 --> 00:09:21,332
[scoffs softly]

128
00:09:22,500 --> 00:09:23,877
Okay, fine.

129
00:09:25,378 --> 00:09:27,213
[in English] Okay. [grunts]

130
00:09:27,297 --> 00:09:28,298
My key.

131
00:09:29,340 --> 00:09:30,383
[in Korean] Right, your key.

132
00:09:34,470 --> 00:09:35,513
[scoffs]

133
00:09:36,055 --> 00:09:37,140
[key card slaps on table]

134
00:09:42,520 --> 00:09:44,355
That hurts, you asshole.

135
00:09:47,275 --> 00:09:48,318
[sighs in exasperation]

136
00:09:51,863 --> 00:09:54,157
Let's shake hands one last time.

137
00:09:57,952 --> 00:09:59,787
I'm moving abroad.

138
00:10:00,705 --> 00:10:03,374
I can't live here
after the way you humiliated me.

139
00:10:03,458 --> 00:10:04,500
[exhales softly]

140
00:10:08,922 --> 00:10:10,131
[♪ music turns ominous]

141
00:10:13,009 --> 00:10:14,427
[laughing maliciously]

142
00:10:14,510 --> 00:10:15,678
[♪ music increases in tempo]

143
00:10:16,471 --> 00:10:17,472
Jin Isoo.

144
00:10:18,973 --> 00:10:19,974
Enjoy the fall.

145
00:10:23,978 --> 00:10:25,647
You're finished.

146
00:10:25,730 --> 00:10:27,023
[♪ music resumes tempo]

147
00:10:28,358 --> 00:10:29,734
[dull, distorted audio]

148
00:10:39,494 --> 00:10:40,995
[high-pitched tone droning]

149
00:10:41,079 --> 00:10:43,122
-[♪ music swells, fades]
-[muffled thuds]

150
00:10:43,206 --> 00:10:46,125
-[audio normalizes]
-[Younghwan laughing maliciously, echoes]

151
00:10:46,209 --> 00:10:47,502
[♪ somber, suspenseful music playing]

152
00:10:47,585 --> 00:10:48,586
[chair squeaks]

153
00:10:48,670 --> 00:10:49,796
[sighs in despair]

154
00:10:49,879 --> 00:10:51,214
That's all?

155
00:10:53,007 --> 00:10:55,802
I don't remember anything after that.
I think I passed out.

156
00:10:55,885 --> 00:10:57,470
[Kyungjin] How can you not remember?

157
00:10:58,137 --> 00:11:00,056
You're... [sighs softly]

158
00:11:00,139 --> 00:11:01,891
This is driving me crazy, too.

159
00:11:02,850 --> 00:11:04,519
How on earth did this happen?

160
00:11:05,770 --> 00:11:06,813
[door bursts open]

161
00:11:06,896 --> 00:11:08,314
[Taegyun] What the hell is going on?

162
00:11:08,398 --> 00:11:09,524
[♪ music fades]

163
00:11:09,607 --> 00:11:10,608
[exhales deeply]

164
00:11:14,237 --> 00:11:16,739
Joo Hyera. I told you, didn't I?

165
00:11:16,823 --> 00:11:18,658
I said he was going to cause trouble!

166
00:11:19,617 --> 00:11:20,660
[exclaims incredulously]

167
00:11:21,744 --> 00:11:22,829
You kept defending him.

168
00:11:23,663 --> 00:11:26,624
A police detective killed someone.
How are you going to fix this?

169
00:11:26,708 --> 00:11:29,168
-We still need to investigate.
-Investigate what?

170
00:11:29,252 --> 00:11:32,422
Jin Isoo and the victim were
the only ones inside the house!

171
00:11:32,505 --> 00:11:34,382
[♪ somber, suspenseful music playing]

172
00:11:35,591 --> 00:11:38,303
Hand over the case
to the Metropolitan Detective Unit.

173
00:11:39,095 --> 00:11:40,471
And you, come with me!

174
00:11:41,389 --> 00:11:42,390
[Taegyun scoffs softly]

175
00:11:45,310 --> 00:11:46,894
-[door slams]
-[sighs softly]

176
00:11:48,855 --> 00:11:50,064
[Kyungjin sighs heavily]

177
00:11:51,232 --> 00:11:52,317
Jin Isoo.

178
00:11:52,400 --> 00:11:55,028
You need to get it together
and remember anything you can.

179
00:11:57,196 --> 00:11:58,364
[sighs grimly]

180
00:12:00,658 --> 00:12:01,659
Where is Jin Isoo?

181
00:12:01,743 --> 00:12:03,077
[♪ tense, foreboding music playing]

182
00:12:06,581 --> 00:12:07,915
What are you going to do?

183
00:12:07,999 --> 00:12:10,793
We're arresting him without a warrant.
He has money and power.

184
00:12:10,877 --> 00:12:12,211
SEOUL METROPOLITAN POLICE
KANG MUJIN

185
00:12:12,295 --> 00:12:13,713
No one's a bigger flight risk.

186
00:12:14,964 --> 00:12:16,341
Go and bring him out.

187
00:12:16,424 --> 00:12:17,967
-[detective 1] Yes, sir.
-[detective 2] Yes, sir.

188
00:12:20,845 --> 00:12:21,929
[♪ music increases in tempo]

189
00:12:22,013 --> 00:12:23,014
[detective 1] Come with us.

190
00:12:23,723 --> 00:12:24,766
[Isoo grunts softly]

191
00:12:26,267 --> 00:12:27,268
[sighs softly]

192
00:12:35,318 --> 00:12:36,986
[Mujin] Mr. Jin Isoo,

193
00:12:37,070 --> 00:12:39,822
you are under arrest
for the murder of Kim Younghwan.

194
00:12:39,906 --> 00:12:43,201
You have the right to an attorney
and the right to remain silent.

195
00:12:43,284 --> 00:12:46,412
You won't be penalized
for remaining silent.

196
00:12:46,496 --> 00:12:48,623
You'll have a chance to explain yourself.

197
00:12:48,706 --> 00:12:50,291
[♪ music swells]

198
00:12:50,375 --> 00:12:52,794
I'm sure you know from playing detective.

199
00:12:54,754 --> 00:12:55,755
Let's go.

200
00:12:57,423 --> 00:13:00,051
Please go out the back.
There are reporters outside.

201
00:13:00,134 --> 00:13:01,177
[♪ music fades]

202
00:13:06,641 --> 00:13:08,559
It really does pay to be a chaebol.

203
00:13:08,643 --> 00:13:11,396
How much will I get for that favor?
Maybe 100 million won?

204
00:13:11,479 --> 00:13:13,064
[♪ somber, suspenseful music playing]

205
00:13:16,484 --> 00:13:17,735
He's not the killer.

206
00:13:18,361 --> 00:13:20,696
He would never kill anyone.

207
00:13:20,780 --> 00:13:21,823
[sighs softly]

208
00:13:21,906 --> 00:13:25,034
How much has he been slipping you
to make you say crap like that?

209
00:13:25,993 --> 00:13:28,329
You should worry about yourselves.

210
00:13:28,413 --> 00:13:30,164
Internal Affairs will be here soon.

211
00:13:31,666 --> 00:13:32,708
Let's go.

212
00:13:35,044 --> 00:13:36,295
[door opens]

213
00:13:36,963 --> 00:13:38,047
[scoffs softly]

214
00:13:38,506 --> 00:13:39,549
[door closes]

215
00:13:43,427 --> 00:13:45,263
[camera shutters clicking]

216
00:13:45,346 --> 00:13:47,557
[reporter 1] Is it true
that you murdered someone?

217
00:13:47,640 --> 00:13:49,475
[reporter 2] Is it true
that the victim was a friend?

218
00:13:49,559 --> 00:13:52,103
-[reporter 3] Why did you kill him?
-[reporter 4] Mr. Jin Isoo!

219
00:13:52,186 --> 00:13:53,354
Do you admit to the murder?

220
00:13:53,437 --> 00:13:55,481
-[reporter 5] Was the murder premeditated?
-[reporter 6] Do you admit to it?

221
00:13:55,565 --> 00:13:56,941
[reporters clamoring]

222
00:13:57,024 --> 00:13:58,442
[♪ tense, somber music playing]

223
00:14:05,283 --> 00:14:06,993
[clamoring continues]

224
00:14:07,076 --> 00:14:08,911
-[reporter 6] Mr. Jin Isoo!
-[siren blaring]

225
00:14:08,995 --> 00:14:09,996
[reporter 7] Mr. Jin Isoo!

226
00:14:11,122 --> 00:14:12,290
[clamor subsides]

227
00:14:13,374 --> 00:14:14,375
What do we do?

228
00:14:16,919 --> 00:14:18,004
[♪ music fades]

229
00:14:18,087 --> 00:14:19,839
[♪ pulsating ominous music playing]

230
00:14:41,861 --> 00:14:44,155
-[cell phone vibrating]
-[♪ music fades]

231
00:14:44,238 --> 00:14:46,824
JUNYOUNG

232
00:14:46,908 --> 00:14:48,993
-[line ringing, connects]
-[Dr. Yoon] <i>Junyoung.</i>

233
00:14:49,785 --> 00:14:51,662
Did you see the body?

234
00:14:52,288 --> 00:14:54,457
[Dr. Yoon] Yes,
I'm looking at him right now.

235
00:14:56,334 --> 00:14:58,419
He was stabbed without hesitation.

236
00:14:59,420 --> 00:15:01,464
Did Detective Jin really do this?

237
00:15:02,632 --> 00:15:04,383
Absolutely not.

238
00:15:04,467 --> 00:15:05,676
It wasn't Isoo.

239
00:15:07,511 --> 00:15:08,596
[sighs softly]

240
00:15:09,096 --> 00:15:11,098
[♪ suspenseful, ticking music playing]

241
00:15:11,933 --> 00:15:13,476
[Mujin] How do you know Kim Younghwan?

242
00:15:16,520 --> 00:15:18,147
You're old friends

243
00:15:18,231 --> 00:15:20,149
and started a production company together?

244
00:15:21,275 --> 00:15:22,360
Yes.

245
00:15:22,818 --> 00:15:24,528
But you arrested him for doing drugs.

246
00:15:27,031 --> 00:15:28,074
[sighs wearily]

247
00:15:28,157 --> 00:15:31,869
He couldn't get off drugs,
so I turned him over to Narcotics.

248
00:15:33,120 --> 00:15:34,372
You're a good friend.

249
00:15:35,623 --> 00:15:37,250
But Kim Younghwan must've been mad.

250
00:15:37,959 --> 00:15:39,377
His friend had betrayed him.

251
00:15:39,460 --> 00:15:40,920
[♪ music increases in tempo]

252
00:15:41,003 --> 00:15:44,257
<i>Kim Younghwan entered your home</i>
<i>at 9:00 p.m. and waited for you.</i>

253
00:15:47,218 --> 00:15:48,469
[card reader beeps]

254
00:15:48,552 --> 00:15:50,096
You had a fight, didn't you?

255
00:15:51,180 --> 00:15:53,099
Things weren't exactly
pleasant between us.

256
00:15:53,182 --> 00:15:54,558
I told him to just leave.

257
00:15:54,642 --> 00:15:56,936
If you had a fight,
why did you do drugs together?

258
00:15:57,019 --> 00:15:58,062
[♪ music fades]

259
00:15:58,145 --> 00:15:59,188
Drugs?

260
00:16:01,691 --> 00:16:03,067
[♪ pulsating foreboding music playing]

261
00:16:03,150 --> 00:16:04,819
[Mujin] This is the drug test
you just took.

262
00:16:04,902 --> 00:16:07,780
Judging by the levels,
you were completely out of it yesterday.

263
00:16:07,863 --> 00:16:08,906
NARCOTICS DETECTED

264
00:16:11,033 --> 00:16:12,243
I don't do drugs.

265
00:16:12,326 --> 00:16:13,703
Then how do you explain this?

266
00:16:15,371 --> 00:16:16,414
[sighs in despair]

267
00:16:18,541 --> 00:16:20,042
Jin Isoo.

268
00:16:20,126 --> 00:16:21,252
Enjoy the fall.

269
00:16:22,503 --> 00:16:23,671
You're finished.

270
00:16:24,755 --> 00:16:26,215
[dull, distorted audio]

271
00:16:26,299 --> 00:16:27,508
[muffled thuds]

272
00:16:27,591 --> 00:16:29,927
A drug that can be absorbed
through skin contact.

273
00:16:30,011 --> 00:16:31,262
I think that's what got me.

274
00:16:31,929 --> 00:16:35,141
I don't remember anything
after shaking hands with Younghwan.

275
00:16:35,224 --> 00:16:36,517
[scoffs]

276
00:16:36,600 --> 00:16:38,311
Are you claiming diminished capacity?

277
00:16:38,394 --> 00:16:39,729
It's the truth.

278
00:16:40,354 --> 00:16:43,441
My team found a drug called "Ruby"
during one of our investigations.

279
00:16:46,360 --> 00:16:47,987
I think it was a similar drug.

280
00:16:49,447 --> 00:16:50,614
[sighs heavily]

281
00:16:51,782 --> 00:16:52,825
[♪ music fades]

282
00:16:52,908 --> 00:16:56,037
We're both detectives here,
so let's be honest.

283
00:16:56,120 --> 00:16:57,621
[♪ gentle, melancholy music playing]

284
00:16:57,705 --> 00:16:59,623
Imagine you're the detective in charge.

285
00:17:00,291 --> 00:17:02,918
Only the victim and the suspect
were present on site.

286
00:17:03,002 --> 00:17:04,962
The two of them are friends,

287
00:17:05,629 --> 00:17:08,215
but the suspect got the victim
convicted on drug charges.

288
00:17:09,717 --> 00:17:10,968
It's enough for a grudge.

289
00:17:11,719 --> 00:17:14,513
The victim was mad
and entered the suspect's home.

290
00:17:14,597 --> 00:17:16,515
The victim died,

291
00:17:17,391 --> 00:17:19,435
and the suspect was high on drugs.

292
00:17:21,103 --> 00:17:22,646
That's not all.

293
00:17:22,730 --> 00:17:25,107
The suspect is a chaebol
who does whatever he wants,

294
00:17:25,191 --> 00:17:28,152
and he carries the trauma
of having both his parents murdered.

295
00:17:30,279 --> 00:17:31,656
What do you think?

296
00:17:32,573 --> 00:17:34,158
He looks guilty to you too, right?

297
00:17:36,619 --> 00:17:37,953
It really wasn't me.

298
00:17:38,037 --> 00:17:40,373
Then why did Kim Younghwan die?
Did he kill himself?

299
00:17:41,832 --> 00:17:43,209
You said someone reported it.

300
00:17:43,292 --> 00:17:45,086
Are you investigating them?

301
00:17:45,169 --> 00:17:46,170
[scoffs]

302
00:17:47,046 --> 00:17:48,047
I am.

303
00:17:48,130 --> 00:17:49,298
Who is it?

304
00:17:49,882 --> 00:17:51,425
You can listen to it yourself.

305
00:17:54,720 --> 00:17:57,890
[Isoo, over recording]
<i>Hello? Please get the police here.</i>

306
00:17:57,973 --> 00:17:59,934
<i>I killed someone.</i>

307
00:18:00,017 --> 00:18:01,477
[dispatcher] <i>Sir, what is your name?</i>

308
00:18:02,603 --> 00:18:04,021
[Isoo] <i>Jin Isoo.</i>

309
00:18:04,814 --> 00:18:06,899
<i>I'm at my house.</i>

310
00:18:06,982 --> 00:18:08,025
[scoffs]

311
00:18:08,526 --> 00:18:09,527
What?

312
00:18:10,111 --> 00:18:11,487
Got nothing left to argue?

313
00:18:11,570 --> 00:18:13,030
[♪ music increases in tempo]

314
00:18:20,621 --> 00:18:22,748
-[Mr. Choi exhales sharply]
-[Mujin sighs]

315
00:18:22,832 --> 00:18:23,833
[♪ music resumes tempo]

316
00:18:23,916 --> 00:18:26,502
I'm done here, so feel free to talk.

317
00:18:32,800 --> 00:18:34,051
[door closes]

318
00:18:35,219 --> 00:18:36,387
[Mr. Choi sighs softly]

319
00:18:37,012 --> 00:18:38,013
[♪ music fades]

320
00:18:38,097 --> 00:18:40,307
[Changun] Don't get involved
and just stay put.

321
00:18:40,391 --> 00:18:42,935
And make sure Park and Choi
don't do anything stupid.

322
00:18:45,563 --> 00:18:47,982
Internal Affairs will be here.
If anything goes wrong,

323
00:18:48,065 --> 00:18:49,650
all your careers are over.

324
00:18:50,860 --> 00:18:53,028
-Leave it with the Metropolitan Unit.
-I can't.

325
00:18:53,112 --> 00:18:54,613
[♪ somber, suspenseful music playing]

326
00:18:54,697 --> 00:18:56,407
They already have a story worked out.

327
00:18:56,490 --> 00:18:58,576
They won't consider
any other possibilities.

328
00:19:02,955 --> 00:19:04,749
Jin Isoo killing someone?

329
00:19:05,499 --> 00:19:06,667
I don't believe it.

330
00:19:06,751 --> 00:19:08,335
You never know with people.

331
00:19:09,003 --> 00:19:10,588
Jin Isoo could be the killer.

332
00:19:11,255 --> 00:19:12,590
Even if that's true,

333
00:19:13,674 --> 00:19:14,967
I need to see it for myself.

334
00:19:15,050 --> 00:19:16,135
Hey, Joo Hyera.

335
00:19:16,218 --> 00:19:17,219
Sir.

336
00:19:18,888 --> 00:19:21,932
If I were in this situation,
would you stand by and do nothing?

337
00:19:23,225 --> 00:19:24,226
[sighs wearily]

338
00:19:28,898 --> 00:19:31,901
For now, there is a way
to prevent him from being detained.

339
00:19:32,443 --> 00:19:34,195
We can dispute this warrantless arrest.

340
00:19:34,278 --> 00:19:35,738
[Isoo] Please don't do that.

341
00:19:38,866 --> 00:19:40,075
I'm a police detective.

342
00:19:41,702 --> 00:19:43,996
I can't use a legal loophole
to run away from this.

343
00:19:44,079 --> 00:19:45,122
Isoo.

344
00:19:45,956 --> 00:19:47,291
This isn't the time for that.

345
00:19:47,374 --> 00:19:48,375
[Isoo] Mr. Choi.

346
00:19:51,295 --> 00:19:52,797
I didn't do it.

347
00:19:54,298 --> 00:19:56,008
I need to catch...

348
00:19:57,343 --> 00:19:58,636
whoever did this.

349
00:20:04,975 --> 00:20:06,143
[Mr. Choi sighs heavily]

350
00:20:06,227 --> 00:20:07,436
[♪ music fades]

351
00:20:07,520 --> 00:20:10,815
<i>Detective Jin Isoo of Gangha Police,</i>
<i>known for being a chaebol heir,</i>

352
00:20:10,898 --> 00:20:12,691
<i>has been arrested on a murder charge.</i>

353
00:20:12,775 --> 00:20:15,861
<i>Police reportedly made</i>
<i>a warrantless arrest</i>

354
00:20:15,945 --> 00:20:18,405
<i>after the victim's body was found</i>
<i>inside his home.</i>

355
00:20:18,489 --> 00:20:20,783
<i>With public attention focused on this case</i>

356
00:20:20,866 --> 00:20:22,868
<i>involving the family</i>
<i>that owns Hansu Group,</i>

357
00:20:22,952 --> 00:20:26,121
<i>police are investigating the circumstances</i>
<i>surrounding the incident.</i>

358
00:20:27,122 --> 00:20:29,083
[news anchor] <i>Detective Jin Isoo,</i>
<i>the chaebol heir</i>

359
00:20:29,166 --> 00:20:30,501
<i>currently working as a detective,</i>

360
00:20:30,584 --> 00:20:32,419
<i>was arrested on suspicion of murder.</i>

361
00:20:32,503 --> 00:20:33,754
<i>What exactly transpired?</i>

362
00:20:33,838 --> 00:20:37,091
[reporter] <i>Yes, a body was found</i>
<i>inside the home of Detective Jin Isoo.</i>

363
00:20:37,174 --> 00:20:39,760
<i>Detective Jin Isoo was</i>
<i>the only person inside the house,</i>

364
00:20:39,844 --> 00:20:43,514
<i>and an arrest warrant was issued after</i>
<i>multiple pieces of evidence were found.</i>

365
00:20:43,597 --> 00:20:46,475
<i>He is currently being questioned</i>
<i>by Seoul Metropolitan Police.</i>

366
00:20:46,559 --> 00:20:48,185
Isoo's gotten himself into trouble.

367
00:20:48,269 --> 00:20:49,645
[♪ suspenseful, pulsating music playing]

368
00:20:58,195 --> 00:21:01,532
[Younghwan, laughing] <i>Look who's here!</i>

369
00:21:01,615 --> 00:21:03,617
My friend, Jin Isoo!

370
00:21:03,701 --> 00:21:06,662
As for me, I thought about you a lot.

371
00:21:07,746 --> 00:21:10,124
What would happen

372
00:21:10,207 --> 00:21:13,335
if the great Jin Isoo ended up in prison?

373
00:21:13,419 --> 00:21:15,713
Let's shake hands one last time.

374
00:21:15,796 --> 00:21:17,214
[laughing maliciously]

375
00:21:18,591 --> 00:21:20,259
-[heavy thud]
-Jin Isoo.

376
00:21:20,342 --> 00:21:21,510
<i>Enjoy the fall.</i>

377
00:21:25,514 --> 00:21:26,682
[♪ music fades]

378
00:21:28,684 --> 00:21:31,020
SEOUL GANGHA POLICE STATION

379
00:21:36,567 --> 00:21:37,610
[door closes]

380
00:21:37,693 --> 00:21:39,737
Detective Joo, what do we do?

381
00:21:41,030 --> 00:21:42,406
[Junyoung] Let's investigate it ourselves.

382
00:21:42,489 --> 00:21:44,074
There's no way Isoo did this.

383
00:21:44,950 --> 00:21:46,201
[Kyungjin] We need to do something.

384
00:21:46,285 --> 00:21:50,414
There's too much evidence against him.
If this goes to trial now, he's finished.

385
00:21:50,497 --> 00:21:52,708
[breathes deeply]
Getting worked up won't help.

386
00:21:52,791 --> 00:21:53,959
You two should stay put.

387
00:21:54,043 --> 00:21:55,544
Are you going to do this alone?

388
00:21:58,005 --> 00:21:59,214
[sighs softly]

389
00:21:59,298 --> 00:22:01,759
What are you all whispering about?

390
00:22:01,842 --> 00:22:04,845
-[door closes]
-You three look way too suspicious.

391
00:22:06,680 --> 00:22:09,224
Are you going to investigate
Jin Isoo's case?

392
00:22:10,309 --> 00:22:11,310
Hey,

393
00:22:11,393 --> 00:22:15,606
if you three make a move, don't you think
that will draw attention, huh?

394
00:22:17,691 --> 00:22:20,361
We'll look into it quietly.

395
00:22:20,444 --> 00:22:21,779
[♪ quirky music playing]

396
00:22:22,696 --> 00:22:23,697
[Junyoung] What?

397
00:22:24,657 --> 00:22:27,368
Hey, Jin Isoo may be a pain,
but at the end of the day,

398
00:22:27,451 --> 00:22:28,661
he's one of our own.

399
00:22:30,913 --> 00:22:33,248
Then, please get us the forensics report,

400
00:22:33,332 --> 00:22:36,919
the vehicle log at the time of the crime,
and the building's security footage.

401
00:22:37,503 --> 00:22:40,506
Oh, you always have a plan, Detective Joo.

402
00:22:40,589 --> 00:22:41,799
Okay, got it.

403
00:22:42,925 --> 00:22:45,094
Will you be able to manage all of that?

404
00:22:45,177 --> 00:22:46,887
What do you take me for, you punk?

405
00:22:47,596 --> 00:22:50,307
Do you know how many
connections I have in this field?

406
00:22:50,391 --> 00:22:51,809
In the world of police,

407
00:22:52,476 --> 00:22:53,811
I'm basically an influencer.

408
00:22:55,854 --> 00:22:56,897
[♪ music fades]

409
00:22:59,233 --> 00:23:00,234
[♪ foreboding music playing]

410
00:23:00,317 --> 00:23:01,777
We're from Internal Affairs.

411
00:23:02,653 --> 00:23:04,989
Senior Inspector Joo Hyera,
Inspector Park Junyoung,

412
00:23:05,072 --> 00:23:08,033
Senior Police Officer Choi Kyungjin.
Come with us.

413
00:23:22,548 --> 00:23:23,882
[♪ music swells, fades]

414
00:23:23,966 --> 00:23:27,177
Did you know
Detective Jin Isoo is a drug addict?

415
00:23:29,013 --> 00:23:30,014
No.

416
00:23:30,097 --> 00:23:31,640
Drugs were found in his system.

417
00:23:31,724 --> 00:23:33,100
A fairly large amount.

418
00:23:33,684 --> 00:23:36,645
How could you work with him and not know?

419
00:23:36,729 --> 00:23:38,022
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

420
00:23:38,105 --> 00:23:39,106
[Kyungjin] <i>Drugs?</i>

421
00:23:39,189 --> 00:23:41,525
No. He'd never do such a thing.

422
00:23:42,192 --> 00:23:43,736
Someone must've drugged him.

423
00:23:43,819 --> 00:23:45,320
This was a setup!

424
00:23:45,404 --> 00:23:46,905
Anger-management issues?

425
00:23:47,656 --> 00:23:50,034
He arrested his half-brother,
who killed his parents.

426
00:23:50,117 --> 00:23:51,827
If it were me, I would've killed him.

427
00:23:51,910 --> 00:23:55,205
Then did you know
he was seeing a psychiatrist?

428
00:23:56,749 --> 00:23:57,875
No, I didn't know.

429
00:23:57,958 --> 00:24:01,879
After his mother was murdered, he was
receiving treatment for a very long time.

430
00:24:02,379 --> 00:24:03,589
You didn't know that either?

431
00:24:03,672 --> 00:24:05,257
I didn't know.

432
00:24:06,800 --> 00:24:07,926
Besides, that fact

433
00:24:08,719 --> 00:24:10,387
has nothing to do with this case.

434
00:24:10,471 --> 00:24:12,347
Why wouldn't it?

435
00:24:13,432 --> 00:24:16,602
I'm saying Jin Isoo is mentally ill.

436
00:24:16,685 --> 00:24:18,270
Please watch what you say.

437
00:24:18,854 --> 00:24:21,774
[inhales sharply] Maybe you knowingly
cleaned things up for him.

438
00:24:22,983 --> 00:24:24,068
He paid you, didn't he?

439
00:24:24,151 --> 00:24:25,152
[scoffs softly]

440
00:24:27,780 --> 00:24:28,781
No, he didn't.

441
00:24:29,448 --> 00:24:33,619
We'll be looking into your bank accounts,
so bear that in mind.

442
00:24:33,702 --> 00:24:35,037
[♪ gentle, somber music playing]

443
00:24:35,120 --> 00:24:36,455
What I really want to know

444
00:24:37,081 --> 00:24:38,791
is why Senior Inspector Joo Hyera,

445
00:24:38,874 --> 00:24:41,668
an elite officer who climbed
the ranks in record time,

446
00:24:41,752 --> 00:24:43,295
went to Gangha Police Station

447
00:24:44,088 --> 00:24:46,590
to play gofer for a chaebol.

448
00:24:47,508 --> 00:24:51,470
[inhales sharply] Did he promise you
a cushy job down the line?

449
00:24:52,137 --> 00:24:53,305
Jin Isoo

450
00:24:54,348 --> 00:24:57,267
is a capable and responsible detective.

451
00:25:00,646 --> 00:25:03,023
Someone who's narrow-minded

452
00:25:03,732 --> 00:25:05,067
won't be able to see that.

453
00:25:08,987 --> 00:25:10,030
[♪ music fades]

454
00:25:13,867 --> 00:25:15,077
EXECUTIVE DIRECTOR SEO JOOHEE

455
00:25:15,160 --> 00:25:16,453
EXECUTIVE DIRECTOR KIM JINSEO

456
00:25:17,079 --> 00:25:18,247
CHAIRMAN CHOI JEONGHUN

457
00:25:18,330 --> 00:25:19,414
PRESIDENT JIN MYUNGJAE

458
00:25:19,498 --> 00:25:20,707
BOARD CHAIR KUK MINGYUN

459
00:25:20,791 --> 00:25:22,751
[♪ suspenseful, pulsating music playing]

460
00:25:44,022 --> 00:25:46,024
As you all know,

461
00:25:46,108 --> 00:25:48,610
Detective Jin Isoo was arrested
on a murder charge,

462
00:25:49,319 --> 00:25:51,530
so we have called
an emergency board meeting.

463
00:25:52,739 --> 00:25:54,533
Did he actually kill someone?

464
00:25:56,368 --> 00:25:57,953
It's still under investigation,

465
00:25:59,246 --> 00:26:00,998
but I don't believe he did.

466
00:26:01,707 --> 00:26:04,543
I'm not asking what you think, Chairman.

467
00:26:04,626 --> 00:26:09,298
Guilty or not, our company's reputation
is going to take a nosedive!

468
00:26:09,381 --> 00:26:14,428
The public is saying we're a company of
murderers owned by a family of murderers.

469
00:26:15,012 --> 00:26:17,806
Why did he have to go out there
to play detective, huh?

470
00:26:17,890 --> 00:26:20,517
He already caused trouble
with that bombing incident.

471
00:26:20,601 --> 00:26:23,729
You've known him since he was a child.
Didn't you see this coming?

472
00:26:24,771 --> 00:26:27,816
The Jin Isoo I know
would never do something like this.

473
00:26:28,817 --> 00:26:30,694
Until the investigation is concluded,

474
00:26:31,904 --> 00:26:33,113
I ask for your patience.

475
00:26:33,197 --> 00:26:37,117
How can you say that
when they have all the evidence?

476
00:26:37,201 --> 00:26:38,744
That's not all.

477
00:26:38,827 --> 00:26:42,456
Detective Jin Isoo used
Hansu Air Space's high-altitude UAV

478
00:26:42,539 --> 00:26:44,499
for personal purposes.

479
00:26:44,583 --> 00:26:46,043
[all murmuring]

480
00:26:48,086 --> 00:26:49,421
Did you know about this?

481
00:26:50,214 --> 00:26:51,215
Yes.

482
00:26:52,090 --> 00:26:53,717
I authorized it.

483
00:26:53,800 --> 00:26:55,135
What?

484
00:26:55,219 --> 00:26:57,179
[murmuring continues]

485
00:26:57,262 --> 00:26:58,263
[Mr. Choi] I apologize.

486
00:26:59,181 --> 00:27:00,682
What on earth...

487
00:27:00,766 --> 00:27:03,477
The press will be all over this.

488
00:27:03,560 --> 00:27:04,811
What are you going to do?

489
00:27:05,562 --> 00:27:06,647
It would seem

490
00:27:07,314 --> 00:27:10,400
we need someone to take responsibility.

491
00:27:10,484 --> 00:27:11,485
[♪ music swells]

492
00:27:13,987 --> 00:27:15,072
Please step down.

493
00:27:15,155 --> 00:27:16,156
[♪ music fades]

494
00:27:16,240 --> 00:27:18,617
I heard you're not even
in the best of health.

495
00:27:18,700 --> 00:27:20,535
[♪ gentle, melancholy music playing]

496
00:27:25,374 --> 00:27:26,541
-[Mr. Choi clears throat]
-[♪ music fades]

497
00:27:32,005 --> 00:27:33,799
-[Mingyun] Great job today.
-[IA investigator] You too.

498
00:27:38,428 --> 00:27:41,306
DETECTIVE DIVISION

499
00:27:41,390 --> 00:27:43,475
What's going to happen to Detective Jin?

500
00:27:43,558 --> 00:27:46,603
What do you think?
The case will go to prosecutors on Monday.

501
00:27:46,687 --> 00:27:47,729
What?

502
00:27:47,813 --> 00:27:50,107
You mean you already
concluded the investigation?

503
00:27:50,190 --> 00:27:53,276
The drugs, the weapon, the fingerprints.

504
00:27:53,360 --> 00:27:55,153
There's more than enough evidence.

505
00:27:55,862 --> 00:27:57,781
If Jin Isoo isn't the real culprit,

506
00:27:58,490 --> 00:27:59,825
if he was set up,

507
00:28:00,826 --> 00:28:02,411
how will you answer for this?

508
00:28:02,494 --> 00:28:04,413
I'll answer for it, in my own way.

509
00:28:04,496 --> 00:28:05,747
So you three

510
00:28:05,831 --> 00:28:08,834
should also answer
for all the crimes you've committed.

511
00:28:08,917 --> 00:28:10,377
[♪ tense music playing]

512
00:28:10,460 --> 00:28:11,920
Let's go.

513
00:28:12,462 --> 00:28:14,006
[♪ music increases in tempo]

514
00:28:17,801 --> 00:28:19,094
[keys jingling]

515
00:28:19,177 --> 00:28:20,178
[♪ music fades]

516
00:28:20,262 --> 00:28:21,513
[lock clicks open]

517
00:28:21,596 --> 00:28:22,639
[gate latch clanks]

518
00:28:24,433 --> 00:28:26,268
Mr. Jin Isoo, you have a visitor.

519
00:28:35,944 --> 00:28:36,945
Isoo!

520
00:28:39,156 --> 00:28:40,574
What are you doing here?

521
00:28:40,657 --> 00:28:43,118
I was worried about you.

522
00:28:43,201 --> 00:28:44,536
What on earth happened?

523
00:28:51,334 --> 00:28:52,753
Did you really

524
00:28:53,587 --> 00:28:55,630
kill Younghwan?

525
00:28:56,715 --> 00:28:58,091
No, I didn't.

526
00:29:00,218 --> 00:29:01,428
Are you sure you didn't?

527
00:29:01,511 --> 00:29:03,597
[♪ suspenseful, foreboding music playing]

528
00:29:12,481 --> 00:29:13,482
I had a feeling

529
00:29:14,524 --> 00:29:16,151
this day would come.

530
00:29:17,694 --> 00:29:19,529
From the first day I met you.

531
00:29:23,033 --> 00:29:24,242
And about Seungju.

532
00:29:25,077 --> 00:29:29,206
I couldn't understand
why you didn't kill him.

533
00:29:30,040 --> 00:29:31,500
He murdered your parents.

534
00:29:32,167 --> 00:29:35,170
You probably had
plenty of opportunities to kill him.

535
00:29:39,466 --> 00:29:40,967
What are you talking about?

536
00:29:43,011 --> 00:29:44,471
I'm not like you.

537
00:29:44,554 --> 00:29:45,639
Are you sure?

538
00:29:47,099 --> 00:29:49,142
Weren't you holding back all this time?

539
00:29:50,769 --> 00:29:52,938
Then you took it all out on Younghwan.

540
00:29:54,940 --> 00:29:56,191
Think back carefully.

541
00:29:56,942 --> 00:30:00,779
Remember how good it felt
when you stabbed Younghwan.

542
00:30:01,530 --> 00:30:03,031
That's who you are.

543
00:30:04,991 --> 00:30:06,451
Stop talking nonsense and go.

544
00:30:07,035 --> 00:30:08,161
[thud]

545
00:30:11,748 --> 00:30:12,999
Don't run away from this.

546
00:30:15,418 --> 00:30:18,672
Once you accept it,
you'll finally be free.

547
00:30:24,219 --> 00:30:27,681
After all, you're my Little Prince.

548
00:30:35,147 --> 00:30:36,148
[♪ music fades]

549
00:30:40,235 --> 00:30:41,903
[Byungsik] This guy, Kim Younghwan.

550
00:30:41,987 --> 00:30:45,031
He didn't do much
after he was released from prison.

551
00:30:45,115 --> 00:30:46,825
And the security footage?

552
00:30:46,908 --> 00:30:48,201
Here you go.

553
00:30:49,035 --> 00:30:50,745
And this is the forensics report.

554
00:30:50,829 --> 00:30:52,414
CRIME SCENE FORENSICS REPORT

555
00:30:52,497 --> 00:30:54,791
And here's the list of vehicles.

556
00:30:54,875 --> 00:30:57,043
You got these really quickly. Thank you.

557
00:30:57,127 --> 00:31:00,547
We should get Jin Isoo out of there.
He grew up pampered.

558
00:31:01,173 --> 00:31:03,216
I bet he's crying right about now.

559
00:31:03,300 --> 00:31:04,551
[chuckles softly]

560
00:31:07,387 --> 00:31:08,430
[gate latch clanks]

561
00:31:11,933 --> 00:31:13,602
[inmate exhales, sniffles]

562
00:31:14,978 --> 00:31:15,979
[groans softly]

563
00:31:16,730 --> 00:31:17,772
[gate clicks]

564
00:31:19,065 --> 00:31:20,192
[gate latch clanks]

565
00:31:20,275 --> 00:31:21,860
-[keys jingle]
-[lock clicks]

566
00:31:23,069 --> 00:31:25,697
Excuse me, sir. Sir!

567
00:31:25,780 --> 00:31:27,157
Can I get something to eat?

568
00:31:27,240 --> 00:31:29,451
I'm starving to death!

569
00:31:30,118 --> 00:31:31,578
You're so mean.

570
00:31:32,704 --> 00:31:33,705
[sniffles sharply]

571
00:31:33,788 --> 00:31:34,789
[exhales softly]

572
00:31:34,873 --> 00:31:35,874
[sniffles sharply]

573
00:31:37,542 --> 00:31:38,585
Jin Isoo.

574
00:31:39,502 --> 00:31:40,503
Flex Cop.

575
00:31:40,587 --> 00:31:41,588
[♪ quirky, suspenseful music playing]

576
00:31:41,671 --> 00:31:42,672
Ah, yes.

577
00:31:44,132 --> 00:31:47,135
Wow. It's great to meet you. I follow you.

578
00:31:47,219 --> 00:31:49,012
Can I get a photo with you?

579
00:31:50,305 --> 00:31:51,640
[laughs heartily]

580
00:31:53,183 --> 00:31:55,185
I don't have my phone.

581
00:31:55,894 --> 00:31:58,104
Sir! Can I borrow your phone?

582
00:31:58,188 --> 00:32:00,106
-To take a picture.
-[guard] Be quiet.

583
00:32:00,899 --> 00:32:02,484
You're so mean.

584
00:32:03,610 --> 00:32:06,780
Bro, then I suppose we could at least...

585
00:32:07,864 --> 00:32:08,865
Let's hug.

586
00:32:13,787 --> 00:32:15,622
[muffled] One second. [sniffles softly]

587
00:32:16,206 --> 00:32:17,874
[gags, retching]

588
00:32:20,543 --> 00:32:21,544
[exhales heavily]

589
00:32:21,628 --> 00:32:22,629
[slurping]

590
00:32:22,712 --> 00:32:23,797
[♪ music fades]

591
00:32:23,880 --> 00:32:26,132
You can still eat
after throwing up like that?

592
00:32:26,549 --> 00:32:28,635
[exhales contentedly] The drugs wore off.

593
00:32:30,220 --> 00:32:31,846
Are you in here for doing drugs?

594
00:32:33,682 --> 00:32:35,767
I can't really remember.

595
00:32:35,850 --> 00:32:38,186
I was having a great time in a club,

596
00:32:39,104 --> 00:32:40,605
and I felt a bit hot,

597
00:32:40,689 --> 00:32:43,024
then they found me on a swing, butt naked.

598
00:32:43,108 --> 00:32:44,484
[chuckling]

599
00:32:45,860 --> 00:32:47,112
By any chance,

600
00:32:47,195 --> 00:32:49,823
do you know a drug
that can be absorbed through the skin?

601
00:32:49,906 --> 00:32:51,491
[♪ gripping, suspenseful music playing]

602
00:32:51,574 --> 00:32:52,993
There's Ruby.

603
00:32:53,952 --> 00:32:56,246
There's also "Touch."
Just by holding it like this,

604
00:32:56,329 --> 00:32:57,664
it gives you an instant kick.

605
00:32:57,747 --> 00:32:59,708
But it's super potent.

606
00:32:59,791 --> 00:33:02,252
That stuff is nasty.

607
00:33:03,211 --> 00:33:04,796
But I don't do that kind of stuff.

608
00:33:04,879 --> 00:33:07,007
If you use that drug for the first time,

609
00:33:07,549 --> 00:33:08,758
can it make you violent?

610
00:33:09,509 --> 00:33:11,219
That's usually what happens.

611
00:33:12,304 --> 00:33:15,598
How should I put this?
People with all those pent-up emotions,

612
00:33:15,682 --> 00:33:18,727
with a lot of negative feelings
end up causing trouble.

613
00:33:19,477 --> 00:33:20,478
The truth is,

614
00:33:21,062 --> 00:33:22,397
when I first did it,

615
00:33:22,480 --> 00:33:25,859
I broke all these windows
and caused a huge scene.

616
00:33:28,862 --> 00:33:29,863
But, bro,

617
00:33:31,072 --> 00:33:33,158
did you do drugs and do something bad?

618
00:33:33,241 --> 00:33:34,451
[♪ music swells]

619
00:33:40,582 --> 00:33:41,791
[♪ music fades]

620
00:33:43,752 --> 00:33:45,670
[♪ tense, foreboding music playing]

621
00:33:52,677 --> 00:33:54,971
[Younghwan] <i>Jin Isoo. Enjoy the fall.</i>

622
00:33:57,307 --> 00:33:59,517
[Younghwan laughing maniacally]

623
00:33:59,601 --> 00:34:00,727
[audio distorts]

624
00:34:10,612 --> 00:34:12,364
[♪ music swells]

625
00:34:13,365 --> 00:34:15,450
[high-pitched tone droning]

626
00:34:15,533 --> 00:34:17,452
[♪ eerie, suspenseful music playing]

627
00:34:21,748 --> 00:34:22,832
[squelch]

628
00:34:22,916 --> 00:34:24,250
[muffled metallic clinking]

629
00:34:26,086 --> 00:34:27,670
[metallic clinking intensifies]

630
00:34:28,713 --> 00:34:30,590
[inmate] What's wrong? Come on, breathe!

631
00:34:30,673 --> 00:34:31,716
[audio normalizes]

632
00:34:31,800 --> 00:34:32,801
Breathe!

633
00:34:32,884 --> 00:34:34,344
[Isoo breathing heavily]

634
00:34:35,303 --> 00:34:36,763
Are you okay?

635
00:34:41,101 --> 00:34:42,894
[♪ soft, suspenseful music playing]

636
00:34:45,980 --> 00:34:47,524
FORENSIC CHEMISTRY REPORT

637
00:34:51,820 --> 00:34:55,365
[Isoo, over recording] <i>Hello?</i>
<i>Please get the police here.</i>

638
00:34:55,448 --> 00:34:57,951
<i>I killed someone.</i>

639
00:34:58,034 --> 00:34:59,703
<i>Jin Isoo.</i>

640
00:34:59,786 --> 00:35:01,037
[mouse clicks]

641
00:35:02,497 --> 00:35:05,834
<i>Hello? Please get the police here.</i>

642
00:35:05,917 --> 00:35:07,210
<i>I killed...</i>

643
00:35:07,293 --> 00:35:09,295
[♪ suspenseful, pulsating music playing]

644
00:35:10,296 --> 00:35:12,465
FORENSIC REPORT
NAME: KIM YOUNGHWAN

645
00:35:14,926 --> 00:35:18,805
[Hyera] <i>The initial stabbing is believed</i>
<i>to have been near the foot of the stairs.</i>

646
00:35:19,806 --> 00:35:21,391
<i>A 5 cm stab wound to the left chest,</i>

647
00:35:21,474 --> 00:35:24,352
<i>2 cm and 4 cm stab wounds</i>
<i>to the left abdomen,</i>

648
00:35:24,436 --> 00:35:27,188
<i>along with defensive wounds</i>
<i>to the left palm.</i>

649
00:35:27,272 --> 00:35:30,442
<i>Defensive wounds on the chest,</i>
<i>abdomen, and hand were found.</i>

650
00:35:30,525 --> 00:35:32,152
-[Younghwan grunts]
-[squelching]

651
00:35:33,445 --> 00:35:34,529
[groans]

652
00:35:36,322 --> 00:35:39,534
[Hyera] <i>The marks suggest</i>
<i>the victim crawled unaided.</i>

653
00:35:40,118 --> 00:35:41,119
[grunts]

654
00:35:41,995 --> 00:35:43,163
-[squelch]
-[Younghwan exclaims]

655
00:35:43,246 --> 00:35:45,373
[Hyera] <i>A 3 cm stab wound</i>
<i>was found on the back.</i>

656
00:35:46,207 --> 00:35:49,377
<i>The victim is believed to have died from</i>
<i>blood loss caused by multiple stab wounds.</i>

657
00:35:51,921 --> 00:35:56,593
<i>Approximately 2.4 m from the resting point</i>
<i>near the stairs to the sofa,</i>

658
00:35:56,676 --> 00:36:00,597
<i>smear marks believed to be</i>
<i>evidence of dragging were found.</i>

659
00:36:00,680 --> 00:36:02,223
[♪ music increases in tempo]

660
00:36:05,477 --> 00:36:06,478
[killer grunts]

661
00:36:06,561 --> 00:36:07,896
[♪ music resumes tempo]

662
00:36:11,691 --> 00:36:12,692
[♪ music fades]

663
00:36:14,861 --> 00:36:15,862
[sighs softly]

664
00:36:15,945 --> 00:36:18,031
[♪ pulsating foreboding music playing]

665
00:36:30,084 --> 00:36:31,628
[doorbell chiming]

666
00:36:35,590 --> 00:36:36,883
[doorbell chiming]

667
00:36:36,966 --> 00:36:38,301
[knocking at door]

668
00:36:39,219 --> 00:36:41,471
[Hyera, over monitor]
<i>I'm with the police. Is anyone home?</i>

669
00:36:47,936 --> 00:36:49,854
-[softly] Oh!
-[♪ music resumes tempo]

670
00:36:49,938 --> 00:36:51,189
Show me your ID.

671
00:36:54,776 --> 00:36:55,944
PUBLIC OFFICIAL ID
JOO HYERA

672
00:36:56,027 --> 00:36:57,987
-Are you really a police officer?
-[♪ music fades]

673
00:36:58,071 --> 00:36:59,948
Yes, I really am.

674
00:37:01,366 --> 00:37:02,367
Come in.

675
00:37:17,340 --> 00:37:18,341
Are you a singer?

676
00:37:19,259 --> 00:37:20,385
Oh... [chuckles]

677
00:37:20,468 --> 00:37:22,720
Yes, that's right. I'm Ko Danbi.

678
00:37:22,804 --> 00:37:23,805
Ah.

679
00:37:25,223 --> 00:37:28,685
Do you know about the incident
that happened next door a few days ago?

680
00:37:29,352 --> 00:37:30,520
I do.

681
00:37:30,603 --> 00:37:33,273
I finally found this house,
but now I have to move again.

682
00:37:33,356 --> 00:37:35,775
[sighs] I don't feel safe
living here anymore.

683
00:37:37,235 --> 00:37:39,237
But why are you handling it like this?

684
00:37:39,320 --> 00:37:42,323
-Sorry?
-I mean, Jin Isoo isn't the killer.

685
00:37:42,407 --> 00:37:43,408
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

686
00:37:43,491 --> 00:37:44,909
What are you talking about?

687
00:37:45,577 --> 00:37:47,871
Someone else went into that house. A man.

688
00:37:50,123 --> 00:37:51,624
How do you know that?

689
00:37:52,959 --> 00:37:55,670
You know what happened
to me last year, right?

690
00:37:57,088 --> 00:37:58,256
Uh... [chuckles]

691
00:37:58,339 --> 00:37:59,716
I'm afraid I don't.

692
00:37:59,799 --> 00:38:00,967
Oh...

693
00:38:01,634 --> 00:38:03,636
I guess you don't read celebrity gossip.

694
00:38:05,096 --> 00:38:08,474
There was this crazy stalker
who was obsessed with me last year.

695
00:38:08,558 --> 00:38:11,895
He hid in the stairwell
every day and watched me,

696
00:38:11,978 --> 00:38:13,813
then eventually broke into my house.

697
00:38:14,564 --> 00:38:17,775
I came home after a performance
to find him lying on my bed.

698
00:38:17,859 --> 00:38:20,570
I moved here because I heard
it was the safest place around,

699
00:38:20,653 --> 00:38:22,113
but I couldn't sleep anymore.

700
00:38:22,655 --> 00:38:25,491
After that, I became an alcoholic.

701
00:38:25,575 --> 00:38:28,870
I'm on medication for anxiety,
and I haven't been able to perform.

702
00:38:30,079 --> 00:38:34,125
[sighs heavily]
It's really easy to ruin someone's life.

703
00:38:36,294 --> 00:38:38,963
But about you seeing someone...

704
00:38:39,047 --> 00:38:40,214
Ah.

705
00:38:40,298 --> 00:38:42,008
There's a sensor in front of my door.

706
00:38:43,635 --> 00:38:45,970
My intercom monitor turns on
when someone walks by.

707
00:38:46,429 --> 00:38:47,513
[monitor beeping]

708
00:38:47,597 --> 00:38:49,307
[♪ gripping, suspenseful music playing]

709
00:39:01,027 --> 00:39:02,612
<i>Around 30 minutes later...</i>

710
00:39:02,695 --> 00:39:03,780
[monitor beeping]

711
00:39:03,863 --> 00:39:05,615
<i>...some guy walked past.</i>

712
00:39:08,242 --> 00:39:09,243
[slurps]

713
00:39:11,287 --> 00:39:12,872
[♪ music increases in tempo]

714
00:39:15,792 --> 00:39:16,918
[♪ music swells]

715
00:39:17,710 --> 00:39:18,711
[♪ music fades]

716
00:39:18,795 --> 00:39:21,506
SEOUL METROPOLITAN POLICE AGENCY

717
00:39:22,215 --> 00:39:23,716
Your hair isn't looking so great.

718
00:39:23,800 --> 00:39:25,718
I didn't wash it.

719
00:39:26,344 --> 00:39:28,721
[chuckles softly] Are you at least eating?

720
00:39:29,973 --> 00:39:31,766
I don't have an appetite.

721
00:39:31,849 --> 00:39:33,393
You should still eat something.

722
00:39:33,476 --> 00:39:35,478
Why do you look so down?

723
00:39:36,145 --> 00:39:37,814
I'm just not used to this place yet.

724
00:39:37,897 --> 00:39:40,024
Why get used to it?
You'll be coming out soon.

725
00:39:41,359 --> 00:39:43,611
The Metropolitan Unit didn't
investigate properly.

726
00:39:46,364 --> 00:39:49,617
In their eyes... [sighs]
...I probably look guilty.

727
00:39:51,160 --> 00:39:52,245
The truth is,

728
00:39:54,414 --> 00:39:56,040
I'm on psychiatric medication.

729
00:39:57,458 --> 00:39:58,459
I know.

730
00:39:59,752 --> 00:40:00,962
You have panic disorder.

731
00:40:02,755 --> 00:40:03,881
If, by some chance,

732
00:40:05,717 --> 00:40:07,719
I really did kill him...

733
00:40:08,678 --> 00:40:09,721
[Hyera] Hey.

734
00:40:09,804 --> 00:40:11,305
Snap out of it.

735
00:40:12,473 --> 00:40:14,726
A few days in lockup
and you've gone all pathetic.

736
00:40:16,728 --> 00:40:17,937
Well, I mean,

737
00:40:19,439 --> 00:40:21,566
I'm not exactly
the most trustworthy person.

738
00:40:22,275 --> 00:40:23,526
Why not?

739
00:40:24,235 --> 00:40:25,695
I trust you.

740
00:40:26,904 --> 00:40:29,991
We believe you're innocent,
and we're still investigating the case.

741
00:40:35,163 --> 00:40:36,831
After you went home,

742
00:40:37,540 --> 00:40:39,250
a man entered your house.

743
00:40:39,333 --> 00:40:40,752
[♪ soft, suspenseful music playing]

744
00:40:40,835 --> 00:40:41,836
A man?

745
00:40:41,919 --> 00:40:43,629
Your neighbor's camera caught him.

746
00:40:45,131 --> 00:40:48,426
You were drugged, then he went inside
and killed Kim Younghwan.

747
00:40:50,011 --> 00:40:51,471
[exhales incredulously]

748
00:40:51,554 --> 00:40:53,014
Are you going to snap out of it?

749
00:40:54,307 --> 00:40:55,308
Yeah.

750
00:40:57,477 --> 00:41:00,021
You just think about
what the killer's after.

751
00:41:01,355 --> 00:41:04,692
Who and why would someone do this?

752
00:41:06,027 --> 00:41:09,322
They could've just killed you,
but put you in here instead.

753
00:41:11,824 --> 00:41:12,825
Okay.

754
00:41:13,951 --> 00:41:15,244
Ah.

755
00:41:15,328 --> 00:41:17,246
Yu Seongwon came here.

756
00:41:17,330 --> 00:41:18,998
[♪ gripping, suspenseful music playing]

757
00:41:20,249 --> 00:41:21,250
Yu Seongwon?

758
00:41:22,126 --> 00:41:23,127
Why?

759
00:41:24,170 --> 00:41:25,171
I don't know.

760
00:41:26,422 --> 00:41:28,591
He told me to accept
that this is who I am.

761
00:41:30,259 --> 00:41:34,514
He looked happy that I was a murderer.

762
00:41:34,597 --> 00:41:35,932
[♪ music increases in tempo]

763
00:41:36,015 --> 00:41:37,141
Could this be

764
00:41:38,226 --> 00:41:40,520
Yu Seongwon's doing?

765
00:41:42,522 --> 00:41:43,731
Yu Seongwon?

766
00:41:46,442 --> 00:41:47,443
Why would he?

767
00:41:47,527 --> 00:41:48,653
[♪ music swells]

768
00:41:52,698 --> 00:41:53,908
[♪ music fades]

769
00:41:55,451 --> 00:41:56,494
[mouse clicks]

770
00:41:56,577 --> 00:41:57,870
[doorbell chiming]

771
00:42:02,125 --> 00:42:03,126
Hyera.

772
00:42:05,086 --> 00:42:06,087
Coffee?

773
00:42:06,170 --> 00:42:08,256
[chuckles softly]
In the middle of the night?

774
00:42:12,385 --> 00:42:14,178
What happened with Detective Jin?

775
00:42:16,639 --> 00:42:17,723
[sighs heavily]

776
00:42:18,349 --> 00:42:19,892
We're still looking into it.

777
00:42:21,894 --> 00:42:24,230
I think he was set up.

778
00:42:26,065 --> 00:42:27,441
[inhales sharply]

779
00:42:27,525 --> 00:42:29,152
Just maybe,

780
00:42:29,235 --> 00:42:30,903
could it have been Yu Seongwon?

781
00:42:31,612 --> 00:42:33,114
-Yu Seongwon?
-Yes.

782
00:42:34,282 --> 00:42:35,867
When he found our cameras,

783
00:42:36,868 --> 00:42:39,996
what if he realized Isoo was on our side
and set the whole thing up?

784
00:42:41,455 --> 00:42:43,875
But he hasn't moved
since breaking our cameras.

785
00:42:43,958 --> 00:42:44,959
Really?

786
00:42:48,004 --> 00:42:49,797
I heard he came to see Jin Isoo.

787
00:42:49,881 --> 00:42:51,883
I followed him that time.

788
00:42:51,966 --> 00:42:54,135
I put a tracker on his car.

789
00:42:54,218 --> 00:42:55,678
[engine roaring]

790
00:42:55,761 --> 00:42:57,346
[♪ pulsating foreboding music playing]

791
00:43:03,436 --> 00:43:04,812
[♪ music swells]

792
00:43:08,816 --> 00:43:10,109
SEOUL METROPOLITAN POLICE AGENCY

793
00:43:13,029 --> 00:43:14,822
YU SEONGWON
STUDIO

794
00:43:14,906 --> 00:43:16,115
[♪ music fades]

795
00:43:19,660 --> 00:43:20,661
What's that?

796
00:43:22,038 --> 00:43:23,247
Ah...

797
00:43:23,331 --> 00:43:27,126
After Detective Jin was arrested,
the high-altitude UAV got disconnected.

798
00:43:27,210 --> 00:43:29,003
-I guess they found out.
-So?

799
00:43:29,086 --> 00:43:31,714
Yours truly went in the middle
of the night to install it.

800
00:43:31,797 --> 00:43:33,716
[♪ gripping, suspenseful music playing]

801
00:43:41,307 --> 00:43:43,142
VIEWCAM

802
00:43:43,226 --> 00:43:45,144
-Why didn't you tell me?
-[♪ music fades]

803
00:43:45,228 --> 00:43:46,604
I figured you'd be busy.

804
00:43:47,855 --> 00:43:49,857
I can handle this much on my own.

805
00:43:49,941 --> 00:43:50,942
[scoffs]

806
00:43:52,568 --> 00:43:54,487
You're really on the ball now.

807
00:43:54,570 --> 00:43:56,447
I'm a one-man operation.

808
00:43:56,530 --> 00:43:57,615
[Minjae chuckles]

809
00:43:58,074 --> 00:44:00,493
Anyway, what did Yu Seongwon say to him?

810
00:44:00,576 --> 00:44:02,828
That he knew Jin Isoo would commit murder.

811
00:44:02,912 --> 00:44:03,996
[♪ ominous music playing]

812
00:44:04,080 --> 00:44:05,164
He found it amusing.

813
00:44:05,873 --> 00:44:07,124
What do you mean?

814
00:44:07,917 --> 00:44:10,711
That's why I thought
maybe Yu Seongwon was behind this.

815
00:44:10,795 --> 00:44:13,172
But this isn't how he does things.

816
00:44:13,256 --> 00:44:15,383
He kidnaps people and kills them.

817
00:44:17,635 --> 00:44:21,347
What does Jin Isoo mean to Yu Seongwon?

818
00:44:22,473 --> 00:44:23,891
That's what I don't get.

819
00:44:23,975 --> 00:44:25,351
You're right.

820
00:44:25,434 --> 00:44:28,187
I think Isoo does mean
something special to him.

821
00:44:29,563 --> 00:44:30,648
[♪ music fades]

822
00:44:31,691 --> 00:44:33,025
What are you going to do now?

823
00:44:34,193 --> 00:44:36,529
We have a suspect,
so we'll have to catch him first.

824
00:44:36,612 --> 00:44:38,197
Call me if you need anything.

825
00:44:38,281 --> 00:44:41,450
[chuckles] Okay. Call me
if anything happens with Yu Seongwon.

826
00:44:42,994 --> 00:44:44,537
Don't act alone again.

827
00:44:45,162 --> 00:44:46,580
Okay, I got it.

828
00:44:46,664 --> 00:44:47,748
[chuckles softly]

829
00:44:49,542 --> 00:44:52,461
SEOUL METROPOLITAN POLICE

830
00:44:52,545 --> 00:44:56,757
SEOUL METROPOLITAN POLICE

831
00:44:58,342 --> 00:45:00,845
DETECTIVE UNIT 1

832
00:45:01,512 --> 00:45:03,973
[detectives chattering, laughing]

833
00:45:07,351 --> 00:45:10,855
[sighs] What do you want this early?
Don't you have work to do?

834
00:45:10,938 --> 00:45:12,857
We came to save you.

835
00:45:14,317 --> 00:45:17,278
You haven't turned Jin Isoo over
to the prosecutors yet, right?

836
00:45:17,361 --> 00:45:18,362
[scoffs]

837
00:45:18,446 --> 00:45:20,614
[♪ gripping, suspenseful music playing]

838
00:45:20,698 --> 00:45:22,867
Thirty minutes after
Detective Jin went inside,

839
00:45:22,950 --> 00:45:25,369
this man went toward his house.

840
00:45:25,453 --> 00:45:27,955
He was caught on the neighbor's camera.

841
00:45:28,748 --> 00:45:30,750
So what? What about this man?

842
00:45:30,833 --> 00:45:32,084
He's a suspect.

843
00:45:32,168 --> 00:45:35,254
I'm saying it's possible
that this man killed Kim Younghwan.

844
00:45:35,338 --> 00:45:36,422
[scoffs]

845
00:45:37,173 --> 00:45:38,758
Are you serious?

846
00:45:38,841 --> 00:45:41,093
How will you prove
that this guy killed him?

847
00:45:42,428 --> 00:45:43,596
We can if we catch him.

848
00:45:43,679 --> 00:45:44,764
[sighs heavily]

849
00:45:45,306 --> 00:45:47,975
Either way, it's true
that Jin Isoo did drugs.

850
00:45:48,059 --> 00:45:51,187
This guy might've been called
to clean up after him.

851
00:45:52,355 --> 00:45:53,522
[Junyoung] That drug

852
00:45:54,315 --> 00:45:57,151
was applied to Detective Jin's hand
by the victim.

853
00:45:57,234 --> 00:45:58,402
[♪ music fades]

854
00:45:59,862 --> 00:46:01,781
[♪ gripping, suspenseful music resumes]

855
00:46:03,616 --> 00:46:05,159
It's a drug called "Touch."

856
00:46:05,242 --> 00:46:07,244
<i>It absorbs right away through the skin,</i>

857
00:46:07,328 --> 00:46:09,205
<i>and Detective Jin was drugged that way.</i>

858
00:46:09,288 --> 00:46:10,289
[camera shutter clicks]

859
00:46:11,374 --> 00:46:13,834
<i>Traces of Touch was found</i>
<i>on the victim's hand.</i>

860
00:46:13,918 --> 00:46:15,836
[camera shutter clicking]

861
00:46:18,422 --> 00:46:20,007
As for the call that came in,

862
00:46:20,758 --> 00:46:23,094
I guess you're not
very familiar with this.

863
00:46:23,177 --> 00:46:25,388
Please listen to it again, carefully.

864
00:46:27,807 --> 00:46:28,891
[♪ music fades]

865
00:46:28,974 --> 00:46:30,309
[Isoo, over recording] <i>Hello?</i>

866
00:46:30,393 --> 00:46:32,520
<i>Please get the police here.</i>

867
00:46:32,603 --> 00:46:34,563
<i>I killed someone.</i>

868
00:46:34,647 --> 00:46:36,565
<i>Jin Isoo.</i>

869
00:46:37,316 --> 00:46:39,944
<i>I'm at my house.</i>

870
00:46:40,694 --> 00:46:42,196
I know. I heard it all.

871
00:46:42,279 --> 00:46:44,740
[exclaims] You don't know.

872
00:46:44,824 --> 00:46:47,201
When you record something,
even if it sounds silent,

873
00:46:47,284 --> 00:46:48,786
it still captures "room tone,"

874
00:46:48,869 --> 00:46:51,205
which is like the hum of a fridge.

875
00:46:51,288 --> 00:46:52,373
But it's not there.

876
00:46:52,456 --> 00:46:54,250
[♪ quirky, dramatic music playing]

877
00:46:54,333 --> 00:46:55,543
In other words, it's fake.

878
00:46:55,626 --> 00:46:58,921
Software's so good these days
that it only takes three minutes to make.

879
00:47:03,801 --> 00:47:05,219
So what?

880
00:47:05,302 --> 00:47:07,638
We've identified the suspect.

881
00:47:08,472 --> 00:47:10,015
If the real killer is caught,

882
00:47:10,975 --> 00:47:11,976
what will happen?

883
00:47:12,059 --> 00:47:14,770
[Kyungjin, clears throat]
The press will have a field day.

884
00:47:14,854 --> 00:47:17,440
That's going to be
really embarrassing for you.

885
00:47:17,523 --> 00:47:20,067
Hansu Group won't just stand by.
They'll sue right away.

886
00:47:20,151 --> 00:47:22,111
Their reputation took a nosedive.

887
00:47:23,154 --> 00:47:24,905
[Kyungjin] That aside,
I'm worried about Isoo.

888
00:47:24,989 --> 00:47:26,782
I bet he's really angry.

889
00:47:26,866 --> 00:47:28,784
I'd lose it, too.

890
00:47:28,868 --> 00:47:31,954
-That would give anyone anger issues.
-[Kyungjin sighs]

891
00:47:33,581 --> 00:47:35,666
I told you I would save you.

892
00:47:36,959 --> 00:47:40,421
I can't do anything about you
facing disciplinary action for negligence,

893
00:47:41,422 --> 00:47:45,509
but I can stop Detective Jin
and Hansu Group from suing you.

894
00:47:47,386 --> 00:47:48,596
[sighs in exasperation]

895
00:47:50,264 --> 00:47:51,682
Please release Jin Isoo.

896
00:47:56,520 --> 00:47:57,521
[♪ music fades]

897
00:48:03,360 --> 00:48:04,862
What's taking so long?

898
00:48:06,489 --> 00:48:09,575
I'm sure Detective Kang is busy
making excuses left and right.

899
00:48:12,995 --> 00:48:13,996
Bro!

900
00:48:14,538 --> 00:48:16,332
[♪ gentle, poignant music playing]

901
00:48:19,793 --> 00:48:21,045
[exhales contentedly]

902
00:48:22,046 --> 00:48:23,589
Did you get out after 10 years?

903
00:48:23,672 --> 00:48:25,508
That's just how I feel.

904
00:48:25,591 --> 00:48:26,926
One day felt like a decade.

905
00:48:27,009 --> 00:48:28,177
[chuckles softly]

906
00:48:28,260 --> 00:48:29,470
You made it through.

907
00:48:30,596 --> 00:48:31,597
Here.

908
00:48:35,768 --> 00:48:37,311
PUBLIC OFFICIAL ID
JIN ISOO

909
00:48:37,394 --> 00:48:38,562
Let's go.

910
00:48:39,480 --> 00:48:40,773
Where are we going?

911
00:48:40,856 --> 00:48:41,941
[Kyungjin] To celebrate.

912
00:48:42,024 --> 00:48:43,067
Celebrating your release.

913
00:48:43,150 --> 00:48:45,736
Ah, not your release,
but for not getting charged.

914
00:48:45,819 --> 00:48:46,904
[scoffs softly]

915
00:48:46,987 --> 00:48:47,988
Let's go, bro.

916
00:48:48,822 --> 00:48:50,157
Don't link arms like this.

917
00:48:50,241 --> 00:48:52,785
-I've been traumatized. Let go.
-[♪ music fades]

918
00:48:53,786 --> 00:48:56,455
Mmm. Mix in the truffle like this.

919
00:48:56,539 --> 00:48:58,374
[exclaims] Mmm!

920
00:48:58,999 --> 00:49:00,167
Hey, slow down.

921
00:49:00,834 --> 00:49:03,254
I haven't eaten in three days.
Look at my hollow eyes.

922
00:49:03,337 --> 00:49:06,882
Isn't it nice, being together like this
and enjoying good food, mmm?

923
00:49:06,966 --> 00:49:07,967
Eat up.

924
00:49:08,592 --> 00:49:09,718
-[sighs deeply]
-[Isoo] Mmm!

925
00:49:12,137 --> 00:49:13,138
[Hyera] Here.

926
00:49:15,099 --> 00:49:16,100
Eat more.

927
00:49:17,935 --> 00:49:19,186
What's this?

928
00:49:19,270 --> 00:49:20,813
Why are you being so nice?

929
00:49:20,896 --> 00:49:22,398
Fine, then don't.

930
00:49:22,481 --> 00:49:23,691
Detective Park, eat up.

931
00:49:23,774 --> 00:49:25,401
Yes, thank you.

932
00:49:25,484 --> 00:49:27,111
This truffle aroma is amazing.

933
00:49:27,194 --> 00:49:30,281
Hey! Give it here. It's mine.

934
00:49:31,240 --> 00:49:33,075
[Kyungjin, grunts]
There's so many people here.

935
00:49:33,158 --> 00:49:34,827
It's become really popular now.

936
00:49:34,910 --> 00:49:36,078
Where did you run off to?

937
00:49:36,161 --> 00:49:37,162
Bro.

938
00:49:38,831 --> 00:49:39,999
Ta-da!

939
00:49:40,082 --> 00:49:41,125
What are you doing?

940
00:49:41,208 --> 00:49:43,043
Just have one bite.
It's bad luck otherwise.

941
00:49:43,127 --> 00:49:44,211
Hey, hey!

942
00:49:45,129 --> 00:49:47,423
I'm already a lucky guy. Super lucky.

943
00:49:48,215 --> 00:49:49,550
-No way.
-Just one bite.

944
00:49:49,633 --> 00:49:50,801
-No!
-Just one bite.

945
00:49:50,884 --> 00:49:52,052
-Open up. Ah...
-[Isoo] Seriously.

946
00:49:52,136 --> 00:49:53,554
[♪ upbeat, jaunty music playing]

947
00:49:53,637 --> 00:49:55,306
You have some, too. Just to be safe.

948
00:49:55,389 --> 00:49:58,058
Eat it as a precaution.
Have more. There you go.

949
00:49:58,142 --> 00:49:59,268
[♪ music fades]

950
00:49:59,351 --> 00:50:01,145
[Hyera] We found the suspect. [sighs]

951
00:50:04,148 --> 00:50:05,524
Cho Pilgu.

952
00:50:05,608 --> 00:50:06,775
Do you know him?

953
00:50:06,859 --> 00:50:09,528
No. How did you find him?

954
00:50:09,612 --> 00:50:12,281
He's a professional. Four prior
convictions, assault and murder.

955
00:50:12,364 --> 00:50:13,699
He's extremely methodical.

956
00:50:13,782 --> 00:50:17,328
He left by subway, so we spent all night
checking footage from all the stations.

957
00:50:17,411 --> 00:50:20,039
He's the one who killed Kim Younghwan.

958
00:50:20,122 --> 00:50:21,582
[♪ tense, pulsating music playing]

959
00:50:23,125 --> 00:50:24,501
[phone clinks]

960
00:50:24,585 --> 00:50:26,086
We'll have to catch him first.

961
00:50:26,712 --> 00:50:28,547
-Stakeout starts tomorrow.
-Got it.

962
00:50:28,631 --> 00:50:30,382
-[in English] Okay. [in Korean] Cheers.
-Got it.

963
00:50:30,966 --> 00:50:32,343
-[Isoo grunts]
-[clinking]

964
00:50:33,385 --> 00:50:34,428
[♪ music fades]

965
00:50:35,012 --> 00:50:36,013
Tomorrow?

966
00:50:37,973 --> 00:50:39,016
All right.

967
00:50:40,768 --> 00:50:41,769
[Isoo] Honk, honk.

968
00:50:44,480 --> 00:50:45,939
Why do you look so serious?

969
00:50:46,315 --> 00:50:47,441
[sighs in relief]

970
00:50:47,524 --> 00:50:49,943
I heard you were released today.

971
00:50:50,027 --> 00:50:51,111
You knew?

972
00:50:51,779 --> 00:50:54,239
Then you should've come with some tofu.

973
00:50:55,115 --> 00:50:56,116
I'm sorry.

974
00:50:56,992 --> 00:50:59,828
I had something going on.

975
00:51:04,083 --> 00:51:05,376
Thank you.

976
00:51:08,921 --> 00:51:10,923
-[sighs softly]
-[Mr. Choi] Mmm.

977
00:51:11,590 --> 00:51:13,967
What happened with the case?

978
00:51:14,968 --> 00:51:16,220
We identified a suspect.

979
00:51:17,596 --> 00:51:20,432
We need to catch the guy
who killed Younghwan.

980
00:51:23,352 --> 00:51:25,729
What was it like in jail?

981
00:51:26,397 --> 00:51:28,357
[sighs heavily] It was the worst.

982
00:51:28,440 --> 00:51:30,901
People were throwing up
and snoring next to me.

983
00:51:30,984 --> 00:51:32,861
Crime really doesn't pay.

984
00:51:32,945 --> 00:51:34,530
Wait, I didn't even commit one.

985
00:51:37,366 --> 00:51:38,992
You've been through a lot.

986
00:51:40,577 --> 00:51:42,162
You're worried about me right now?

987
00:51:43,414 --> 00:51:44,998
I heard they're voting you out.

988
00:51:45,082 --> 00:51:46,083
[♪ melancholy music playing]

989
00:51:46,166 --> 00:51:47,543
Ah... [sighs]

990
00:51:47,626 --> 00:51:48,627
You heard?

991
00:51:49,545 --> 00:51:50,963
What's the reason?

992
00:51:51,046 --> 00:51:52,047
Well...

993
00:51:53,048 --> 00:51:54,049
For various reasons.

994
00:51:55,759 --> 00:51:57,136
It was my uncle, wasn't it?

995
00:51:59,763 --> 00:52:01,223
Unbelievable.

996
00:52:01,306 --> 00:52:03,392
He always tries to worm his way in.

997
00:52:03,475 --> 00:52:05,018
No, you're wrong.

998
00:52:05,936 --> 00:52:07,646
It's just time.

999
00:52:07,730 --> 00:52:09,940
So what, you'll go travel the world?

1000
00:52:10,023 --> 00:52:12,192
You'll shake it all off
and forget all about me?

1001
00:52:12,276 --> 00:52:13,694
[chuckles softly]

1002
00:52:13,777 --> 00:52:16,530
I have to go. It's my dream.

1003
00:52:19,950 --> 00:52:20,951
[sighs softly]

1004
00:52:21,034 --> 00:52:22,035
[♪ music fades]

1005
00:52:24,371 --> 00:52:27,374
[Mingyun] We will now vote
on the motion to remove the CEO.

1006
00:52:27,458 --> 00:52:30,169
All those in favor, raise your hand.

1007
00:52:30,252 --> 00:52:32,254
[♪ tense, suspenseful music playing]

1008
00:52:35,215 --> 00:52:36,300
[sighs softly]

1009
00:52:36,383 --> 00:52:40,512
With this, the motion to remove the CEO,
Mr. Choi Jeonghun, has passed.

1010
00:52:42,514 --> 00:52:43,599
Chairman Choi.

1011
00:52:44,808 --> 00:52:46,769
Thank you for all your hard work.

1012
00:52:48,520 --> 00:52:51,023
Everyone, let's get up and go.

1013
00:52:56,236 --> 00:52:57,362
[♪ music fades]

1014
00:52:57,446 --> 00:53:00,949
It's been a while since I came in,
and there was an important meeting.

1015
00:53:01,617 --> 00:53:03,327
Please, everyone, have a seat.

1016
00:53:05,329 --> 00:53:07,164
-Mr. Kuk.
-[Mingyun] Yes?

1017
00:53:07,247 --> 00:53:08,582
What motion was passed?

1018
00:53:09,291 --> 00:53:11,919
Uh, the motion to remove the CEO.

1019
00:53:12,002 --> 00:53:13,587
-Really?
-[Mingyun] Yes.

1020
00:53:13,670 --> 00:53:14,838
What was the reason?

1021
00:53:15,714 --> 00:53:17,424
He's not in the best of health.

1022
00:53:18,217 --> 00:53:20,636
The surgery went well,
and he's recovering just fine.

1023
00:53:20,719 --> 00:53:21,720
What else?

1024
00:53:21,804 --> 00:53:24,264
Uh, the unauthorized
high-altitude UAV use.

1025
00:53:24,348 --> 00:53:25,599
That was my request.

1026
00:53:25,682 --> 00:53:27,226
[♪ tense, ticking music playing]

1027
00:53:27,309 --> 00:53:28,310
Anything else?

1028
00:53:28,393 --> 00:53:29,394
Uh...

1029
00:53:31,021 --> 00:53:33,065
[♪ upbeat rock music playing]

1030
00:53:33,148 --> 00:53:35,192
It seems after my arrest,

1031
00:53:35,275 --> 00:53:37,903
you were all used by someone
who wants to be the CEO.

1032
00:53:39,988 --> 00:53:42,366
How can I possibly trust this board?

1033
00:53:43,617 --> 00:53:45,369
This isn't your place to interfere.

1034
00:53:48,539 --> 00:53:51,542
As Hansu Group's largest shareholder
and non-executive director,

1035
00:53:53,043 --> 00:53:55,629
I propose a motion to reappoint
Mr. Choi Jeonghun as CEO.

1036
00:53:57,047 --> 00:53:59,007
-Let's vote right away.
-What are you doing?

1037
00:53:59,091 --> 00:54:00,467
[♪ music increases in tempo]

1038
00:54:00,551 --> 00:54:02,052
You think this is a joke?

1039
00:54:02,135 --> 00:54:03,595
All in favor,

1040
00:54:04,304 --> 00:54:05,305
raise your hand.

1041
00:54:13,272 --> 00:54:15,357
It looks like the matter has been settled.

1042
00:54:15,440 --> 00:54:17,234
You should all go. You must be busy.

1043
00:54:28,912 --> 00:54:31,623
They say you get less greedy with age.

1044
00:54:32,499 --> 00:54:34,251
You should really let go now.

1045
00:54:35,002 --> 00:54:37,921
Ah, then again, I do understand.

1046
00:54:38,005 --> 00:54:41,425
Your younger brother always outshone you.
No wonder you're bitter.

1047
00:54:42,301 --> 00:54:43,385
But you should know,

1048
00:54:45,971 --> 00:54:47,848
you're no match for me either, Uncle.

1049
00:54:59,526 --> 00:55:01,486
[♪ electric guitar chord swells]

1050
00:55:04,364 --> 00:55:05,365
[♪ music fades]

1051
00:55:05,449 --> 00:55:06,617
Why did you do that?

1052
00:55:07,367 --> 00:55:10,495
There's no one better suited
to be CEO of Hansu Group than you.

1053
00:55:12,372 --> 00:55:15,459
And I refuse to let you
be pushed out like this because of me.

1054
00:55:15,542 --> 00:55:17,085
[♪ gentle, poignant music playing]

1055
00:55:17,169 --> 00:55:19,963
My uncle's a mean person.

1056
00:55:20,047 --> 00:55:22,257
It'd be bad news
if someone like him became CEO.

1057
00:55:22,341 --> 00:55:23,675
[chuckles]

1058
00:55:23,759 --> 00:55:26,803
I'll personally send you
on that trip myself.

1059
00:55:27,596 --> 00:55:28,597
But until then,

1060
00:55:29,806 --> 00:55:31,308
please look after the company.

1061
00:55:37,564 --> 00:55:39,650
Oh no, I'm late. I'd better go.

1062
00:55:45,697 --> 00:55:47,115
-[sighs heavily]
-[♪ music fades]

1063
00:55:47,699 --> 00:55:48,950
[line ringing]

1064
00:55:53,205 --> 00:55:55,540
-Where is Jin Isoo?
-He won't answer his phone.

1065
00:55:55,624 --> 00:55:57,292
[automated voice]
<i>The number you have dialed...</i>

1066
00:55:57,376 --> 00:55:59,419
-[in English] I'm back.
-Bro.

1067
00:55:59,503 --> 00:56:01,171
What are you wearing?

1068
00:56:01,254 --> 00:56:02,839
[in Korean] I had to stop by somewhere.

1069
00:56:02,923 --> 00:56:04,633
-Are you a trot singer?
-Close enough.

1070
00:56:05,384 --> 00:56:08,220
Cho Pilgu is inside his house.
There on the second floor.

1071
00:56:09,054 --> 00:56:11,765
Detective Park and I will go up.
You stay out of sight.

1072
00:56:11,848 --> 00:56:13,975
Okay, fine. I'll hide near the entrance.

1073
00:56:14,059 --> 00:56:15,477
-Me too.
-[Isoo] Okay.

1074
00:56:15,560 --> 00:56:18,105
[♪ gripping, foreboding music playing]

1075
00:56:18,188 --> 00:56:20,482
Cho Pilgu is dangerous.
We have to be careful.

1076
00:56:20,565 --> 00:56:22,192
-Got it.
-Got it.

1077
00:56:25,696 --> 00:56:27,322
[♪ music increases in tempo]

1078
00:56:40,001 --> 00:56:41,169
[doorbell chiming]

1079
00:56:45,382 --> 00:56:46,591
[Junyoung] I'm from the post office.

1080
00:56:46,675 --> 00:56:48,135
[Pilgu] What do you want?

1081
00:56:49,928 --> 00:56:52,347
Am I speaking to Mr. Cho Pilgu?

1082
00:56:52,431 --> 00:56:55,934
I have a court document
that has to be delivered to you in person.

1083
00:56:58,687 --> 00:57:00,105
[♪ music resumes tempo]

1084
00:57:00,188 --> 00:57:01,523
Could you sign right here?

1085
00:57:08,864 --> 00:57:09,990
[♪ music increases in tempo]

1086
00:57:10,073 --> 00:57:11,533
[Junyoung and Kyungjin grunting]

1087
00:57:13,118 --> 00:57:14,286
[Junyoung grunts, groans]

1088
00:57:14,953 --> 00:57:15,954
Cho Pilgu.

1089
00:57:18,415 --> 00:57:19,624
-[Pilgu grunts]
-[shattering]

1090
00:57:20,041 --> 00:57:21,585
[Pilgu grunts, exhales heavily]

1091
00:57:24,963 --> 00:57:26,381
-Hey, Cho Pilgu.
-[glass shard scrapes]

1092
00:57:27,924 --> 00:57:29,009
-[Pilgu grunts]
-[fabric rips]

1093
00:57:30,010 --> 00:57:31,928
You asshole. This is expensive.

1094
00:57:32,512 --> 00:57:34,181
[both panting]

1095
00:57:34,890 --> 00:57:36,141
-[Junyoung grunts]
-[Kyungjin swears softly]

1096
00:57:36,224 --> 00:57:37,476
[Hyera panting]

1097
00:57:42,647 --> 00:57:43,815
[cycle clatters]

1098
00:57:49,738 --> 00:57:50,781
-[grunts]
-[shattering]

1099
00:57:50,864 --> 00:57:52,032
[Isoo groans]

1100
00:57:57,078 --> 00:57:58,538
[panting]

1101
00:57:58,622 --> 00:57:59,915
[♪ music resumes tempo]

1102
00:58:01,917 --> 00:58:03,210
[grunts, panting]

1103
00:58:03,293 --> 00:58:04,920
[♪ gripping, foreboding music continues]

1104
00:58:06,755 --> 00:58:08,215
[exhales, panting]

1105
00:58:14,596 --> 00:58:16,139
[continues panting] Oh, oh...

1106
00:58:18,892 --> 00:58:20,310
[Isoo continues panting]

1107
00:58:23,480 --> 00:58:25,065
Kid, go inside.

1108
00:58:25,148 --> 00:58:26,525
Go inside!

1109
00:58:28,902 --> 00:58:29,986
[exhales anxiously]

1110
00:58:32,072 --> 00:58:33,281
Your heart's pounding.

1111
00:58:33,365 --> 00:58:34,491
[♪ music increases in tempo]

1112
00:58:34,574 --> 00:58:36,243
[kid breathing shakily]

1113
00:58:37,452 --> 00:58:38,453
Drop the knife.

1114
00:58:38,537 --> 00:58:39,704
[♪ music swells]

1115
00:58:51,341 --> 00:58:52,384
[♪ music fades]

1116
00:58:52,467 --> 00:58:53,468
FLEX X COP 2
EPISODE 11

1117
00:58:53,552 --> 00:58:54,886
THE CHASE COMES TO A HEAD

1118
00:58:54,970 --> 00:58:56,555
[♪ upbeat pop music playing]

1119
00:59:19,494 --> 00:59:22,956
Special Cast. Min Kyoungah

1120
00:59:30,005 --> 00:59:31,381
Why did you kill Younghwan?

1121
00:59:31,464 --> 00:59:32,883
[Kyungjin] <i>Cho Pilgu collapsed!</i>

1122
00:59:32,966 --> 00:59:34,467
[Isoo] <i>But I can't see the bigger picture.</i>

1123
00:59:34,551 --> 00:59:36,261
[Junyoung] <i>Forensics didn't find anything.</i>

1124
00:59:36,344 --> 00:59:37,888
You think you're perfect, don't you?

1125
00:59:37,971 --> 00:59:40,849
I'm working on a new piece.
Would you like to see?

1126
00:59:41,600 --> 00:59:43,351
Are you going to trust someone like her?

1127
00:59:43,435 --> 00:59:44,519
You shut your mouth.

1128
00:59:44,603 --> 00:59:46,396
You have no manners.
You should be careful.

1129
00:59:47,230 --> 00:59:49,774
I think we'll have to kill him.

1130
00:59:49,858 --> 00:59:51,443
<i>Find someone.</i>

1131
00:59:51,526 --> 00:59:52,694
I'm a lawyer.

1132
00:59:52,777 --> 00:59:54,696
[Seongwon] <i>Make him cause an accident.</i>

1133
00:59:54,779 --> 00:59:55,947
It's going to be so much fun.

1134
00:59:56,031 --> 00:59:57,282
Where's Detective Joo?

1135
00:59:57,365 --> 00:59:58,783
How did we get a body delivered?

1136
00:59:59,659 --> 01:00:01,161
[gasps, sobbing]

1137
01:00:02,829 --> 01:00:04,039
[♪ music fades]

1138
01:00:06,750 --> 01:00:07,751
[cell phone vibrating]

1139
01:00:09,544 --> 01:00:10,962
[♪ suspenseful, ominous music playing]

1140
01:00:19,304 --> 01:00:21,056
[cell phone continues vibrating]

1141
01:00:27,228 --> 01:00:28,313
[Pilgu] Mr. Lawyer.

1142
01:00:29,189 --> 01:00:30,899
I've been caught.

1143
01:00:32,150 --> 01:00:33,318
[sighs softly]

1144
01:00:36,029 --> 01:00:37,739
[whispering] You'd better hurry.

1145
01:00:47,666 --> 01:00:49,668
Translated by Hyesoo Lee

